<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>62.0</apiVersion>
    <assignments>
        <name>SetVehicleIdFromQuote</name>
        <label>Assignment: Set Vehicle Id from Quote</label>
        <locationX>200</locationX><locationY>200</locationY>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>vehicleId</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value><stringValue></stringValue></value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <connector><targetReference>GetQuotedVehicle</targetReference></connector>
        <description>TODO-DAVI: replace the empty value with the $Record field that links the quoted unit (Vehicle/VIN) in the GRPQM guided selling model. While empty, the guard does not block anything. If a Quote Before Handler flow already exists in the org, MERGE this logic into it (one before-handler per object, per GRPQM conventions).</description>
    </assignments>
    <customErrors>
        <name>BlockDemoUnitSale</name>
        <label>Custom Error: Block Demo Unit Sale</label>
        <locationX>200</locationX><locationY>500</locationY>
        <customErrorMessages>
            <errorMessage>Esta unidad está designada como Demo/Exhibición y no puede cotizarse en la venta general (HU-046). Si necesita venderla, solicite la liberación a su gerente.</errorMessage>
            <isFieldError>false</isFieldError>
        </customErrorMessages>
    </customErrors>
    <decisions>
        <name>IsUnitBlocked</name>
        <label>Decision: Unit Designated as Demo?</label>
        <locationX>200</locationX><locationY>400</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Allow</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>UnitBlocked</name>
            <conditionLogic>1 AND (2 OR 3)</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>GetQuotedVehicle</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue><booleanValue>false</booleanValue></rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>GetQuotedVehicle.Status</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue><stringValue>En demostración</stringValue></rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>GetQuotedVehicle.Status</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue><stringValue>En exhibicion</stringValue></rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector><targetReference>BlockDemoUnitSale</targetReference></connector>
            <label>Blocked</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>HasBypassPermission</name>
        <label>Decision: Has Bypass Permission?</label>
        <locationX>200</locationX><locationY>100</locationY>
        <defaultConnector><targetReference>SetVehicleIdFromQuote</targetReference></defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Validate</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>BypassGranted</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Permission.BypassAllocationValidation</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue><booleanValue>true</booleanValue></rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <label>Bypass (integration/admin)</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Sales guard for demo/exhibition vehicles, no Apex (HU-046, Esc.10 - visible but not sellable). All countries. Before-save on Quote creation: if the quoted unit has Vehicle.Status = En demostración or En exhibicion, a custom error blocks the quote (also protects quotes created outside guided selling). DESIGN NOTE 05/08: SerializedProduct.Status is a system-restricted picklist (custom values NOT allowed - verified in org), so the guard pivoted from SerializedProduct.Status=Allocated to Vehicle.Status. Bypass via BypassAllocationValidation custom permission. Picklist API values used verbatim from the org: En demostración (accented), En exhibicion (NOT accented).</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>Quote Before Handler {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Flow Trigger: Quote Before Handler</label>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>GetQuotedVehicle</name>
        <label>Get Records: Get Quoted Vehicle</label>
        <locationX>200</locationX><locationY>300</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector><targetReference>IsUnitBlocked</targetReference></connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value><elementReference>vehicleId</elementReference></value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>Vehicle</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <start>
        <locationX>200</locationX><locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector><targetReference>HasBypassPermission</targetReference></connector>
        <object>Quote</object>
        <recordTriggerType>Create</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordBeforeSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Draft</status>
    <variables>
        <name>vehicleId</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <isCollection>false</isCollection><isInput>false</isInput><isOutput>false</isOutput>
    </variables>
</Flow>
